# A zero-width rule fires whenever its guards hold, so one whose guards
# hold only where an earlier one's do never fires.
# error: lexer_zero_width_shadowed.grammar:10:1:
# error: this rule can never match: whenever its guards hold, the zero-width rule on line 9 fires first
@lexer
tokens
    a, b, c, eof, err
'c'                             → c
@ pre > 0                       → a
@ pre > 1                       → b
.                               → err

@parser
top! = ERR → 1
